From man cc:
NOTES

  The standard library, /usr/ccs/lib/libc.a or /usr/shlib/libc.so, is loaded
  by using the -lc loader option and not a full path name.  The wrong one
  could be loaded if there are files with the name libc.{so,a} string in the
  directories specified with the -L loader option or in the default direc-
  tories searched by the loader.


The compile line:
  cc -L/usr/lib hello.c

will produce an a.out that seg. faults before entering user code, even
for the classic ``hello world'' program.

This is because ld at run time grabs /usr/lib/libc.a before
it even tries /usr/shlib/libc.so .

all of
  cc -L/usr/lib -non_shared hello.c
  cc hello.c
  cc -L/usr/shlib -L/usr/lib hello.c
  gcc -L/usr/shlib -L/usr/lib hello.c
  gcc -L/usr/lib -static hello.c
  gcc hello.c
work as expected and produce runnable code.

  cc -L/usr/lib hello.c
  gcc -L/usr/lib hello.c
produce executable that seg fault in the morecore called before main.

-- 
               Peter B.G. Mayo  <pbgmayo@watcgl.UWaterloo.Ca>


