Those should be

if (cp != NULL)
        printf("cp is not NULL, but -> %ld\n", cp);
printf("Cp is %lu\n", cp);

remember, sizeof (char *) > sizeof (int).  %d interprets the object
as an int, which only shows you half of cp.  Similarly, *ip only sets
half of cp, as you'll discover when you get the printf() formats right.

In short, not a compiler bug.

