I'm running on an Alpha with DEC's OSF v1.3a, and I've built tcsh 6.04 with
"config.decosf1".  I still have an intermittent problem with pipes:

	> ls -lgAF | more

	Suspended (tty output)
	[1] 25232 25233
	> jobs -l
	[1]  + 25232 Done                   ls -lgAF |
	       25233 Suspended (tty output) more

Bringing the job into foreground gets you "hung", where ^C/^Z won't work,
and you must then kill off the "more" from another process.  It's an annoyance
for me, but will be a major pain for our users.

Has anyone built "tcsh" differently to avoid this problem?  I never use the
"stty tostop" stuff, so it's not that.  It seems to be some sort of timing
