Definitely not the correct data. This got broken in OSF/1 R1.0.3, though
prior to that (R1.0 through R1.0.2) it didn't work at all (cputimes were never
reported). This was fixed (correctly) in our sources around Feb 1992, and
released in OSF/1 R1.1. (It missed the R1.0.4 maintenance release).

Since DEC OSF/1 V1.3 is based on OSF/1 R1.1, they should have the correct
code. With source, it's an easy change: the call to ruadd() from exit() should
be moved from 2 lines above the call to acct() to just below it. If DEC
wants a reference to verify the change against, it is our Change Request 
number 4537.


