It's interesting to note that the pc noted above (^^) stands for 
"program counter", ie, the address where the code is generating these
exceptions.  

This means you can set a breakpoint at that address in dbx, run the
code, type "where" when it stops, and find out the routine and line
number that generated the unaligned access.  Unless, of course, the 
executable has been stripped.  Hope this helps.

