If you are doing a port of toolkit layer stuff, you may want to note
that there is an issue with properties that occasionally stings the
toolkit layers but is rarely an issue with client programs.

With XChangeProperty and XGetWindowProperty, if the format == 32, then
the data is expected to be arrays of unsigned longs and NOT unsigned
ints. This interpretation was made with the blessing of the X Cons.
and is one of the few areas of change that had to be made that was not
just sizeof(int) <> sizeof(long) related.

Note that Xlib "does the right thing" with the data in the longs, that
is is transmits only the significant 32 bits in XChangeProperty and 
expands (pads) to 64 bits in XGetWindowProperty. 

/Dave


