>
>	1). What impact will this have performance-wise?  We are running
>	real-time applications on DEC Alpha OSF 1.3; my concern is that
>	this kind of stuff will bring the system to its knees.

If you're concerned about overrunning other processes in CPU, lower
your own priority, if you're concerned about pushing the systems
I/O system, "throttle" you write traffic, i.e. do the append-writing
in a timed loop and insert some usleeps in between

>	2). Assuming that the system can handle this kind of onslaught,
>	is there a recommended way of processing this kind of data

18 MByte every 30 minutes isn't a lot, so just use normal stdio functions.

>	3). Does it make any sense to keep this information in a separate
>	file system, in terms of performance?  How about on another node,

It makes sense in terms of disk space :-).

