Hi,
	Some of you have mailed me asking why you are getting "file ln0 not
found" when invoking ether/interman.  I've been told that the OSF/1 packetfilter
configuartion is identical to the Ultrix config.  It also seems as though
OSF/1 does not have the packetfilter configured into the kernel by default -
so those of you who cannot get the netman stuff working because of this
oversight will have to perform the following steps:

	* Edit your kernel config file (/usr/sys/conf/mips/<HOSTNAME> under
	  Ultrix), and look for:

		options         PACKETFILTER
		pseudo-device   packetfilter

	  If you cannot find these entries, add them.

	* Configure and build a new kernel (doconfig -c <HOSTNAME> under Ultrix)

	* # cd /dev
	* # MAKEDEV pfilt

For a more thorough description do a "man packetfilter".

